WEBVTT

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:17.080
Kimizuka, what you said
yesterday was true... wasn't it?

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.420
Aren't you here right now
because you believed me?

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.670
I guess so.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:25.340
Is there something you're uneasy about?

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:30.760
Nothing in particular;
I just feel vaguely dissatisfied.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.800
About what?

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.220
About the fact that you're
trying to solve this case,

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.310
even though I'm the detective.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:41.940
That's just how it happened
to play out this time.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.480
The day will come when
you'll be saving my butt.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.400
Up until now, I was exclusively
in that position.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.910
If I don't do some of the work, that heart
of yours will get upset with me.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.080
It's just about curtain time.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.750
What? You do care, don't you?

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:05.420
Only about the job.
I said that yesterday, too.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:09.470
That's what you said, but does
acting account for all of that?

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:12.090
You were super icky yesterday.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.260
Don't call me "super icky."

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.350
A high school girl saying
"super icky" is as hurtful as it gets.

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:22.640
Anyway, this is no time for trifling talk.
Hurry it up a little.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.940
I do want to be there
in time for Eight-One.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.440
You <i>are </i>obsessed, aren't you?

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:34.820
Episode 4

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:43.580
We said we needed a helping hand,
but it's already down to just us two...

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:47.090
As long as it got us in, it was enough.

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:50.510
They're short-handed over there as well;
we can't get everything we want.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:54.680
I guess... So the "them"
you've talked about--

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:57.300
if they're hiding somewhere, then where?

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.060
I don't know.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:02.020
They could be among the spectators,

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:06.900
or it's also possible they're hiding
in the wings like that guy yesterday.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:11.570
You should've left that in the cab;
aren't you hot?

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:14.110
Yeah, a little.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:25.500
♬ It may be the taste of a perfect
and wonderful steak ♬

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.500
L.O.V.E. Yu-ri-<i>nyan</i>!

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:30.880
♬ A mystery story,
memory of a bittersweet love ♬

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:37.590
♬ My heart pitter-patters, hooked on
the thrill of that grizzly-roar wine ♬

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:42.890
♬ I want a love that's tart and sweet,
raspberry super lovely ♬

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.930
Wow. This is a lot different
from the rehearsal.

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.890
Hey! Where are our seats?

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:47.440
♬ Grizzly--Gonna eat up your
heart with bear power ♬

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:43.890
Hey! Where are our seats?

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:47.440
Why would we have seats?
We don't have tickets!

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:48.730
Right...

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:52.150
For starters, let's look for that good
spot we selected yesterday.

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.820
Huh? Hey, wait up!

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:04.620
Unbelievable... That kid
treats people like trash.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:13.920
Saikawa Yu-ri-<i>nyan</i>!

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.970
Thank you all!

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:21.470
Are you getting fired up?

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:25.230
I can see you all!

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.570
That one song is still to come, right?

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:39.740
Yeah, it's next--after Eight-One.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:44.790
That's right, it was. So yesterday's
rehearsal really was work.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.290
You doubt me too much.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:51.210
If something's going to happen,
it will be during "Sapphire Phantasm."

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:57.300
Since you're fired up,
that means it's time for...

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.970
Here comes Eight-One.
We should hurry up a bit.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.850
Wha--?

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:08.730
Wait, is this--?

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:10.980
The set list changed!

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.860
And you were looking forward
to Eight-One so much!

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:18.030
That's not the issue! Hurry!

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:31.330
♬ Woke up early, still sleepy, but ♬

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:32.460
Yu-ri-<i>nyan</i>!

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:38.590
♬ Opened only one of the curtains ♬

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:43.100
For this song, her biggest hit,
she does a certain performance.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:44.640
♬ The shape of a special feeling ♬

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.560
That's got to be the trigger.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:51.060
♬ Try embracing a feeling
that isn't an illusion ♬

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:50.020
That's right. The wrongdoers' target
isn't actually the sapphire in her vault.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:52.810
They're actually targeting
Saikawa herself.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:57.990
♬ Like a mirror reflecting the blue Earth ♬

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.820
I also have a notion of what
their motive might be.

00:04:55.820 --> 00:05:00.200
There's no time to check every place
where the wrongdoers might be hiding.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:02.780
♬ Let's illuminate the universe's
farthest reaches with light ♬

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.780
In this situation, I just need to get
as close to Saikawa as possible.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:06.030
♬ Sapphire--a glittering stage ♬

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:09.660
♬ Phantasm--beyond all dreams ♬

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:09.660
Even so, there's no guarantee
I'll be able to protect her.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.210
♬ Wanna send out
a resounding melody of love ♬

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.210
Ultimately, unless we find the scumbags...

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:18.260
♬ Let's go--a night sky
shimmering with stars ♬

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:15.750
Where are they? Where?

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:21.010
♬ The rhythm pounding in my chest ♬

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:30.020
♬ Reach your hand out farther;
you can grab the miracle ♬

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:23.550
With this extreme volume,
and the cheering on top of it,

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.810
my ears are completely useless.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:35.060
So if my hearing and vision
aren't functioning well,

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:38.070
it has this much impact
on my brain, too...

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:44.240
♬ Knocking on a brand-new door ♬

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.490
Yu-ri-<i>nyan</i>!

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.450
I'd like to rely on Natsunagi
right now, but in this setting,

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:51.460
♬ Moving forward off and on,
my courage plays hide-and-seek ♬

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:48.870
we can't even communicate

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:51.460
Ultimate cuteness, Yu-ri-<i>nyan</i>!

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:51.460
our intentions at any decent level.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:57.590
♬ Think back to what matters most ♬

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:54.960
Curse it! The noise is such a hindrance.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.590
The noise... That's it!

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:03.930
♬ You shouldn't feel so alone ♬

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:02.220
<i>He </i>could hear even the heartbeat
of an assailant hiding somewhere.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:03.930
It's me! Can you hear me?

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:10.850
♬ Like a wish floating in
the white Milky Way ♬

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.890
Where is the assailant?

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:15.650
♬ Let's fulfill our heart's desires
to the ends of the universe ♬

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.180
Level 2 middle section

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:19.110
♬ Sapphire--even a quiet voice ♬

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:22.280
♬ Phantasm--can be a source of strength ♬

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:27.830
♬ The beat that resonates
will lead us there ♬

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:27.830
Curse it!

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:30.950
♬ Let's go--a night sky
shimmering with stars ♬

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:34.710
♬ The rhythm pounding in my chest ♬

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:43.970
♬ Don't fear it anymore,
the miracle we embrace ♬

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:43.970
The song's big hook is coming up. What Yui
keeps sealed away will be revealed.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:48.350
Yui Saikawa's deepest secret is the thing
that's hidden behind that eyepatch.

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:50.850
The secret she hid from us.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:58.560
♬ The hidden secret is in the jewel-box ♬

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:05.950
♬ A blinding light will burst out ♬

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:04.150
That's right.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:10.830
The Miracle Sapphire worth three
billion yen is Yui Saikawa's left eye.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:10.830
♬ Sapphire--a glittering stage ♬

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.910
♬ Phantasm--beyond all dreams ♬

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.910
Gotta make it in time!

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:19.630
♬ Wanna send out a resounding
melody of love ♬

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:17.330
You! What have you been up to?
Stop right here!

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.630
Saikawa is in danger!

00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:22.630
♬ Let's go--a night sky
shimmering with stars ♬

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:26.380
♬ The rhythm pounding in my chest ♬

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:34.480
♬ Reach your hand out farther;
you can grab the miracle ♬

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:31.510
Kimizuka!

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:34.480
Let me go!

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:41.070
♬ The wide-open future ♬

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:46.740
♬ The scene before our eyes ♬

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:53.160
♬ Overlapping memories ♬

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:59.580
♬ Let's grab the miracle ♬

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.530
Kimizuka-<i>san</i>?

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:37.660
Yui Saikawa-sama

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:41.880
It's all my fault. I hid information
that I should have told you.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:46.880
Umm, I'm not fully
comprehending all this yet.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:48.670
Right...

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:52.800
So first off, I'll start with my left eye.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:57.390
Or, ultimately, that might
be the whole story.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:05.480
Yes, this is a false eye.
From birth, I was blind in my left eye,

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.740
and with the complex I had about it,

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:11.910
I became a very withdrawn,
reflective child.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:16.700
So what my parents gave me was
a sapphire-colored false eye,

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:19.250
bluer than any ocean.

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:23.420
Enchanted by its beauty,
just by having this eye,

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:27.210
I was able to have confidence in myself.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:31.180
It was around that time that I
started to work as a performer.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:36.140
My father and mother were both thrilled
to see how upbeat I'd become.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:40.770
"Ah, this is what being alive feels like."

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:46.480
Maybe you'll laugh at me for exaggerating,
but that's what I thought.

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:54.740
But that life of smooth sailing
didn't last for long.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:10:01.870
Three years ago, when I was 11 years old,
both my parents died in an accident.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:07.290
What they left me was a large house
and an outrageously large fortune.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:11.760
And there was also... this left eye.

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:16.760
So this eye meant more
to me than anything,

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:20.270
and it was something I wanted to keep
close to my heart, just for me.

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:25.100
That's the reason why I've normally
always worn an eyepatch.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:31.320
During my big stage appearances, I would
show this left eye for just one moment.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:36.570
Like saying, "I'm here," wanting
my parents in Heaven to notice.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:41.790
I never imagined in my wildest
dreams that this eye

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:45.170
was being targeted by criminals.

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:47.960
You really lived up to
a detective's reputation.

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:49.880
You saw through my secrets,

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:54.340
realized the criminals' true
target, and saved me.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:11:01.890
I'm so glad I approached the two of you.
Thank you so very, very much.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:05.940
That's enough. Raise your head!

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:12.230
Yes, as an outcome, nobody was harmed,
and the sapphire wasn't stolen...

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:16.530
Thus, the case--the story--
wound toward its conclusion.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:20.410
With that, we probably could have
put this situation behind us...

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:23.410
...if it had been the me
of one week earlier...

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:24.790
However...

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:29.630
...I wasn't going to keep
my eyes closed anymore.

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:30.920
So, Saikawa...

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:32.630
Yes?

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:37.840
Are you not concerned about the penalty
for failing to kill Natsunagi and me?

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:39.090
Huh?

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:55.990
Oh, my. What kind of talk is that
all of a sudden, Mr. Sidekick?

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:00.820
Are you saying I was trying
to kill you two?

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:06.910
Ha! It seems like you'd be better
suited to being a mystery writer.

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:12.880
Come on, Kimizuka. Saikawa-<i>san </i>already
confessed her secret, didn't she?

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:17.220
Even I haven't heard a word from you
about anything beyond that.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:23.680
It's true Saikawa confessed her secret,
but her lie hasn't been revealed yet.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.220
Lie?

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:30.480
Hello? This is Kimizuka.

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:32.820
Things here are safely wrapped up.

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:35.690
Seriously--one nuisance just
keeps piling up on another.

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:40.360
Just as you said, a timed detonator
was rigged up in the vault,

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:43.280
so I had the bomb squad dismantle it.

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:49.160
That was a close call. You would
have been blown to bits by now.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:52.330
Thank you, Fuubi-<i>san</i>.

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:54.210
So there it is.

00:12:56.380 --> 00:13:01.590
B-But the bad guys' target was supposed
to be Saikawa-<i>san</i>'s left eye...

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:04.050
Why would they go after her house, too?

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:11.940
They had two targets. One was Saikawa's
sapphire left eye. But the other...

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:15.020
...was our lives, Natsunagi.

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:16.480
What does this mean?

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:22.450
From the start, Saikawa knew their plan--
well, was informed of their plan--

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:25.410
and was luring us into the vault.

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:27.910
That's just-- Where's the proof?

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:30.290
Fuubi-<i>san </i>said she hadn't heard about it.

00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:31.540
Eh?

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:35.630
About a threating letter having been
delivered to the Saikawa home.

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:45.720
Saikawa contacted you and me, rather than
the police, for some special purpose.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:49.930
Why would Saikawa-<i>san</i>, an idol,
do something like that? She can't be--

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:55.560
No, she doesn't belong to SPES.
Most likely she was being threatened.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:58.110
"If you don't want that left
eye taken from you,

00:13:58.110 --> 00:14:01.860
put an end to Kimihiko Kimizuka."
Something like that.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:05.700
But, Saikawa, they aren't
as easygoing as all that.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:11.410
They tried to take both our
lives <i>and </i>your left eye.

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:17.840
Or, no, perhaps they weren't attempting
to take it so much as destroy it.

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:21.380
But why such an interest
in Saikawa-<i>san</i>'s left eye?

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:26.600
It means there's something about Saikawa's
left eye that SPES is fixated on.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:29.640
Simply put, it's of the same
nature as that guy's ear.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:31.350
That guy...?

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:38.150
That false eye--that artificial left eye--
can see through objects.

00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:40.440
Isn't that right, Saikawa?

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:45.030
What can you see right now?

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.330
Is that for personal defense?

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:50.950
Never underestimate an idol.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:55.120
Being able to keep such a big smile on
your face while knowing I had this...

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.460
Wh-Why?

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.170
I won't hand over my left eye.

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:05.470
Now I get it.

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:06.260
Eh?

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:11.520
Saikawa was deceived by those scum
into thinking you and I were her enemies

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:14.310
and are trying to steal the sapphire.

00:15:14.310 --> 00:15:19.570
And they proposed to her that they'd
lend a hand in dealing with us.

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:23.570
Disgusting--did they also give you that?

00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:27.240
No, I got this on my own initiative.

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:29.620
So how did you know?

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:33.540
Ordinarily, a person with
sight in only one eye

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:36.580
in addition to losing more than
20% of their field of vision,

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.540
also has a harder time gauging distance.

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:41.250
You, on the other hand,

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:44.380
moved around while wearing an eyepatch
without any appreciable impairment.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:49.680
I see. So you didn't trust me
from the start?

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:51.760
I wondered what that was all about

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:54.220
when you said you wanted
to go to the rehearsal.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:56.440
Did you believe I'd become a Yui-<i>nya </i>fan?

00:15:56.440 --> 00:16:01.110
Yes. I thought for sure you were
a captive to my charms.

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:04.570
Yeah, even Natsunagi had
grave doubts about me.

00:16:04.570 --> 00:16:05.650
So, Mr. Sidekick,

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:09.740
was the man dressed in black at the
rehearsal also something you arranged?

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:14.040
You're a sharp one. You see, human beings
show their instinctual reactions

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:15.330
in moments of danger.

00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:20.080
Would someone normally go that far just
to test the functionality of a left eye?

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:23.340
It's the training from my former partner.

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:27.090
So is this it? Are all our cards
now on the table?

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:30.930
Yes. I've now bared all.

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:35.640
Then I'll ask one more thing:
Will you lower that gun for me?

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:37.480
But that's--

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:41.980
You must realize... if I hadn't
rushed at you at that time,

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:45.820
that crossbow bolt would certainly
have taken your left eye.

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:51.160
If I were truly your enemy, would I have
gone to such extremes for you?

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:52.830
But it's--

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:57.750
Listen to me, Saikawa.
Killing us won't help.

00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:03.590
After you've killed us, your left eye will
be taken from you by the real enemy.

00:17:03.590 --> 00:17:05.460
No, it won't!

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:17.390
Honestly... I already know.
I already understand...

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.980
...that you two aren't my enemies.

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:25.900
But how...?

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:30.110
How will I be able to keep my left eye?

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:40.000
I can't. My father and mother
are gone; without this left eye...

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:43.420
...I can't survive all the dark days.

00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:47.460
"That's not true."
Telling her that would be easy.

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:50.840
But just saying that wouldn't save her.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:54.970
She's desperately forged ahead
as an idol amidst the darkness,

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:58.390
and is fighting alone, even now,
with a gun clenched in her hand.

00:17:58.390 --> 00:18:05.980
So what on earth could save her? The thing
she wants most of all. And that's--

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:11.360
Umm, the two of us had plans, once this
case was finished, to go to the seashore.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:18.040
So I was just wondering if you might
come along with us, Saikawa-<i>san</i>.

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:26.210
Meaning, would you be my friend?
That's what I'm trying to say.

00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:32.550
Why? I tried to kill you both.

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:37.510
It's fine. We aren't about
to die that easily.

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:42.100
I-I can't. I don't deserve that.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:44.770
I'm the one who gets
to decide that, right?

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.310
But... But...

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:50.730
I want to be your friend.

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:56.070
Would you indulge me in this?

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:03.960
This... is abnormal, Natsunagi-<i>san</i>.

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:05.120
Is it?

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:07.540
But I'm telling you, having an
abnormal person as a friend

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:09.210
would definitely be fun.

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:11.090
That's what I'm thinking these days.

00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:17.430
Even if... Even if we did become friends,
that wouldn't resolve any problems.

00:19:17.430 --> 00:19:21.310
Just the opposite--I'd end up
causing you needless trouble.

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:23.480
I doubt it.

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:26.850
Huh?

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:33.030
Saikawa, if you say they're targeting you,
well, it's the same for me.

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:35.150
Don't think of it as causing us trouble.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:38.070
On the contrary,
think of us as fellow targets.

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:40.910
Forming a sort of alliance
would be rather advantageous.

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:44.290
You're going... to help me?

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:47.040
Yes. We'll help.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:52.380
So, Saikawa... we want you
to become our compatriot.

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:01.850
Yes, I'd be glad to.

